// #100 HALF C — THE BODY-INJECTION CHANNEL, and the reason it was the priority.
//
// `collect_impl` resolved the impl's trait with `find_trait_iter_scoped` (so it
// registered the USER trait's method list) while `lower_impl_block` resolved it
// with a BARE `traits_.find(trait_name)` (so it read the STDLIB homonym). The
// two disagreeing meant lower_impl_block walked the STDLIB trait's methods and
// synthesised every default-bodied one it did not find overridden INTO THE
// USER'S IMPL — stdlib source text lowered against user types, across a package
// boundary, from a file that never mentions it.
//
// MEASURED on this exact shape before the fix (`nm -C` of the object):
//     T ZqH__is_empty                    ← the stdlib ExactSizeIterator default
//     T test.ZqH__len__f__ref_ZqH        ← the only fn this file declares
// Note the injected symbol is not merely extra: it is emitted UNQUALIFIED and
// UNMANGLED, with no package prefix and no `__f__sig` suffix, so two packages
// doing this collide at the LINKER.
// With `trait Datum` the injected body did not even compile, and the
// diagnostic pointed at LINE 89 OF A 6-LINE FILE:
//     t_Datum.logos:89: error [fn ZqH__from_datum]: unknown type 'DView'
//
// ⚠ THIS FIXTURE DOES NOT BITE, AND SAYING SO IS THE POINT. MEASURED on the
// pre-fix compiler it is GREEN: the stdlib `is_empty` default was lowered and
// EMITTED, but `collect_impl` (already scoped) never registered it for method
// resolution, so nothing in .logos source could call it and no `.expected`
// could see it. The biting admit for this half is
// pass/trait_homonym_default_body_datum.logos (pre-fix: a hard error at line
// 89 of a six-line file); the biting assertion about the EMITTED SYMBOL is the
// gate logos_00_trait_homonym_no_injected_symbol, because an object file's
// symbol table is not something a fixture can read. This file is kept as the
// regression guard for the day the collect side also goes bare.
//
// WHAT IT DOES ASSERT: THE USER'S BODY RAN. `len()` is declared and implemented
// HERE and nowhere else; 20 + 7 = 27 is this file's arithmetic. The stdlib
// `ExactSizeIterator::is_empty` default (`return self.len() == 0`) would have
// been attached to `ZqH` alongside it; the companion fail fixture
// trait_homonym_default_body_injected_fail.logos pins that it is NOT.
package test;
trait ExactSizeIterator { fn len(&self) -> i64; }
struct ZqH { w: i64 }
impl ExactSizeIterator for ZqH { fn len(&self) -> i64 { return self.w + 7i64; } }
fn main() -> i32 { let h = ZqH{w:20i64}; return h.len() as i32; }
